{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>וירק.</b> That he gave them weapons of war, like the sense of \"and draw the spear\" (Psalms 35:3). Others say to draw the sword from its sheath, like the sense of אל הארץ יריקו (Ecclesiastes 11:3), מריקים שקיהם (Genesis 42:35). Also a spear has this [meaning]." "<b>חניכיו.</b> That he trained them many times in war. And if it is not mentioned — and the reckoning of the letters of Eliezer is by way of derash, for Scripture does not speak in gematria, for whoever wishes can make any name out for good or for evil. Rather, the name according to its plain meaning."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:35.566636834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}